      "content": "I get that, but I'm worried that if I just say \"emerging threats\" they'll ask for specifics. If they look closely at the actual audit data, they're going to see there aren't any active vulnerabilities or even any trends indicating a decline in their security. \n\nAre there any specific gaps or \"weaknesses\" we can point to in the report—even if they're minor—to justify why they need the continuous monitoring right now? I need something a bit more concrete than just \"the landscape is shifting.\"",
